        <item>
            <title>Roland GP-100 Patches and Things</title>
            <link>https://ology.github.io/2026/10/04/roland-gp-100-patches-and-things/</link>
            <guid>https://ology.github.io/2026/10/04/roland-gp-100-patches-and-things/</guid>
            <description><![CDATA[
                <p><img alt="Roland GP-100" src="https://ology.github.io/2026/10/04/roland-gp-100-patches-and-things/gp-100.jpg"></p>

<p>I recently acquired a classic, Roland GP-100 guitar effects processor from a friend. He is a wicked guitarist, multi-instrumentalist virtuoso, and owned it for decades. Naturally it&#39;s loaded with custom Jimmy Page and Zappa patches, EVH, Bridge of Sighs, ZZ Top, on and on!</p>

<p>Anyway, I recorded a dump of the GP memory onto an external MIDI track in Logic Pro. I think this is a valid MIDI sysex file of the patches. But I don&#39;t want to test it on this thing, I&#39;ve never tried it before, and I only have one!</p>

<p>But if <strong>you</strong> have it dialed-in, please check <a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1P_XY7moAdn7v3fV3Pe4dd_V0BWqTB19e/view?usp=drive_link">this file</a> out, see if it works (i.e. should have a Zappa patch or two), and tell me if so or if not. :D</p>

<p>Here is a cool <a href="https://www.vintagedigital.com.au/roland-gp-100/">write-up</a> on the device. And here are its <a href="https://support.roland.com/hc/en-us/articles/201946959-GP-100-Technical-Specifications">technical specifications</a>.</p>

<h1>Roland #GP100 #MIDI #SYSEX</h1>


